Duties as city clerk (continued)

2.

To keep correct and full minutes of the proceedings of city council together with all ordinances and resolutions passed by it, in a properly indexed book or register kept for that purpose; :

To receive all applications or petitions made to the city and to place them before the mayor and city council at the meeting of council next succeeding the receipt thereof;

To issue all licenses, and keep a record thereof, and all badges and permits authorized by the council;

To attend all sessions of the Mayor's Court;

To keep an execution docket, in which he shall enter the names of all persons tried and fined by the Mayor's Court, the nature of the offense, date of trial, amount of fine, and return of the police officer thereon;

To issue all summonses, processes and Subponenas to witnesses that may be necessary in the enforcement of this code or other rules, regulations and ordinances of the city council;

To be the custodian of the city seal and affix its impression on documents: whenever required;

To carefully preserve the records and documents belonging to the city which are not assigned to the custody of some other office, md to maintain a proper index to all such records and documents so that ready access thereto and use thereof may be had.

Duties as city treasurer. The city clerk/treasurer shall have the following duties in his capacity as city treasurer:

1.

To receive all money due the city council, including taxes, and pay out the same only upon orders passed by the city council and signed by the mayor, or in his absence, the mayor pro tempore.

To keep a book of accounts showing all money received on behalf of the city and the source and disposition thereof, which book shall be open for inspection by the public and city councilmen;

To keep such other records and accounts as May be required by statute or ordinance;

To furnish the council with statements detailing all receipts and payments of funds for the quarter.

